// **an element is a destination like any other.** all three spellings used to store 2 and say
// nothing: the append reaches its slot through a synthesized operator rather than a written
// declaration, and the ordinary argument conversion narrows - which is right for a variable and is
// silent data loss for a literal.
//
// tests_eco/arrays/literal_lossless_conversion.eco is the other half: a literal that converts
// exactly still converts, silently, because nothing was lost

array<int32> $a = [1, 2.5];

array<int32> $b = [];
$b[] = 2.5;
$b[0] = 3.9;

// the untyped literal is the same defect wearing a disguise - the first element decides the type,
// so this is an array<int32> and 2.5 is appended into it
$c = [1, 2.5];

echo $a[1];
echo $b[0];
echo $c[1];
